      "rank": 1,
      "priority": "MEDIUM",
      "category": "Policy",
      "description": "Recommendation 1: Bundle CPT 59430 into obstetric delivery codes 59400, 59510, 59514, and 59515 for the same pregnancy; deny overlapping maternity claims, and allow separate 59430 only for split obstetrical care in the same delivery episode when billed by a separate physician under a different tax identification number within 60 days postpartum/within 6 weeks of delivery, limited to once per pregnancy (279 days). Peer: Healthfirst, Highmark BCBS, and United Health all place CPT 59430 inside obstetric bundles tied to 59400/59510, and Highmark plus United Health extend cesarean-related guardrails to 59514 and 59515 with split-care or single-period limits..\n\nRecommendation 2: Carve out office E/M 99202-99215 with modifier 24 from the postpartum bundle during the postpartum period when used for evaluation and management of pregnancy complications, rather than auto-denying these visits under CPT 59430. Exempt: modifier 24 for non-OB office E/M, evaluation and management of pregnancy complications.",
